@startuml bootwire_error_status_sequence
!include ../_style.iuml
title <size:21><color:#1B3A5F><b>Error Status</b></color></size>\n<size:13><color:#5B6B7C>the target rejects the request; the host raises the error at once and does not retry</color></size>
!include _participants.iuml

autonumber "<b>00"
APP -> HOST : send(WRITE, address 0x08000000 + data)
note left of HOST
  bootwire write checks the range on the host first.
  A raw "bootwire send" or a buggy host can still
  ask for it, so the target must check too.
end note
HOST -> TP : WRITE [SEQ=0x60, 0x08000000, …]
activate TP
TP -> TP : 0x08000000 < app_start\n→ BAD_PARAM
note right of TP
  Nothing is written: the bootloader
  protects its own flash.
end note
TP --> HOST : [SEQ=0x60, 0x91, <color:#C0392B><b>BAD_PARAM</b></color>]
deactivate TP
HOST -> HOST : STATUS ≠ OK → stop at once\n(a resend would get the same answer)
HOST --> APP : BootWireStatusError(WRITE, <color:#C0392B><b>BAD_PARAM</b></color>)
APP -> APP : print the error, exit code 1
@enduml
